# Reserved names — one per line, `#` starts a comment.
#
# ⛔ None of these may appear in a fixture FILENAME or in a fixture JSON KEY.
# ✅ They are permitted in fixture VALUES: `generator.repo` must name this repository,
#    because a value records origin and is not an identifier.
#
# The reason for the rule: a fixture key and a fixture filename are permanent identifiers.
# Anything that consumes this evidence will carry them for as long as the evidence exists,
# and a project can be renamed. An identifier that encodes a renameable name turns a
# rename into a data migration.
#
# ⚠ Copy this file to `config/reserved-names.txt` and add the names of every consumer.
#    That file is NOT committed — the mechanism belongs in the open, the names of
#    unreleased projects do not. With no local file only the default below applies, and
#    every generator prints that fact before it writes anything.

saakshi
